.TH RESOLVD 8 "" "Peios" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
resolvd \- Peios machine-wide name-resolution service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B resolvd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B resolvd
maintains one DNS policy and cache for native Peios clients, the DNS stub
on 127.0.0.53 port 53, and the libnss_peios_net.so.2 hosts NSS module.
The daemon runs under the Peios service manager. It has no command-line
configuration interface; use the registry and the resolv operator client.
.PP
Live interface servers, search domains, addresses, metrics and routing roles
come from netd. Machine-wide fallback servers and static host names come
from the registry. The daemon does not rewrite /etc/resolv.conf.
The packaged resolver configuration is a constant pointer to the loopback stub.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The daemon reads the registry key
.B Machine\eSystem\eNetwork\eDns
at startup and when it changes.
.TP
.B FallbackServers
Servers used only when no interface contributes servers.
.TP
.B ExtraSearchDomains
Additional search domains applied after interface search domains.
A single-label name without an applicable domain is not sent bare upstream.
.TP
.B ControlSecurity
Security descriptor for the native control socket. RESOLVER_QUERY authorizes
queries and status; RESOLVER_CONTROL authorizes cache flushing.
The compiled default grants query rights to Everyone and all rights to
SYSTEM and Administrators. It applies when this value is absent or malformed.
.TP
.B Hosts
Subkey mapping static host names to one address or several addresses.
Exact case-insensitive matches take precedence over DNS. These names also
apply to reverse queries and to native, NSS, and stub clients.
.PP
See /usr/share/regman/resolvd.regman for value types and full policy details.
.SH SECURITY
The native socket checks each request against the peer's token.
The loopback DNS stub is an anonymous interface: DNS carries no caller
identity, and ControlSecurity does not govern this listener.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/resolvd/resolv.sock
Native request and reply socket.
.TP
.I /usr/etc/resolv.conf
Packaged constant configuration selecting 127.0.0.53.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regim/resolvd-service.reg
Service definition and runtime-directory seed.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regim/resolvd-port.reg
DNS port reservation seed.
.TP
.I /usr/share/regman/resolvd.regman
Registry reference. Peios uses the registry Hosts subkey instead of /etc/hosts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR resolv (1)
